course: dictionary
lesson: 2411
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Cutter» is a good example: it can be a tool, a person, or a boat. Read the sentence around the word to find out which meaning fits.
explain: «One cuts, the other chooses» is a fair way to share a cake. The cutter is the person who cuts the cake. They have every reason to make the two pieces equal, because the other person gets to choose first.
explain: A cutter can also be a thing, like a pastry cutter that presses shapes out of dough. Ask yourself: is this cutter a thing, a person, or a boat? The rest of the sentence will tell you.
fact: A cutter is a tool or machine used for cutting, like a pastry cutter, wire cutters or a paper cutter.
fact: A cutter is also a person whose job is to cut things, like cloth or stone.
fact: A cutter is a small, fast boat or ship used by the coast guard.
fact: «Cookie cutter» can also mean all the same, with nothing original about it.
fact: Razors, craft knives and box cutters are for grown-ups only, because their blades are very sharp and slip easily.
exercise: «Use the pastry cutter to press out star shapes.» What is a pastry cutter? | A small fast boat | A person who makes pastry for a living | A kind of biscuit | *A tool used for cutting shapes
exercise: «The cutter raced out to help the sinking ship.» What is the cutter here? | *A small, fast boat used by the coast guard | A paper cutter | A pair of wire cutters | A person whose job is to cut cloth
exercise: «When one person cuts and the other chooses, the cutter has a reason to cut fairly.» Who is the cutter in this sentence? | The cake itself | *The person who cuts the pieces | The person who chooses a piece | The knife on the table
test: «Wire cutters snipped through the fence.» What kind of cutter is this? | A person who cuts stone | A cookie made in a shape | A boat on the sea | *A tool used for cutting
test: Someone says, «Every house on this street is a cookie cutter.» What do they mean? | They are made of biscuits | They are the newest houses in town | They have very sharp knives inside | *They all look the same, with nothing original
exam: Which meaning fits best in «The cutter at the stone yard shaped each block by hand.»? | *A person whose job is to cut things, like stone | A tool used for cutting paper | A cookie cutter that makes shapes | A small fast boat used by the coast guard
